  "music": "w4-castle-clatter",
  "authorNotes": "Two players, three checkpoints, four segments — every prop and gap type the world has, in one long run. Seg 1: a plain lever-w4-08-warm/door-w4-08-warm (latching) plus swing-w4-08-1 (280px) gets both players moving, same shape as 02. Seg 2 is a crumbly-floor obstacle (material crumbly, render taped per the paper-construction rule — it can be broken, so it's taped, not drawn): the 300px stretch at x1500-1800 crumbles roughly 1.2s after being gripped, so it must be crossed briskly rather than lingered on. crate-w4-08-a (picked up back at pier 2) and crate-w4-08-b (found on the far side of the crumbly stretch) both need to be carried all the way to segment 4 for the plate puzzle — the gauntlet is as much about not dropping cargo across a breaking floor as it is about the floor itself. Seg 3 is a pure timing hazard: crusher-w4-08, a portcullis slab patrolling the doorway at x3060 on a y650-940 path at 90px/s (a slow, clearly telegraphed rhythm, no lever or signal involved — this one is dodged, not solved), followed by swing-w4-08-2 (280px) across the real gap beyond it. Seg 4 is the climax, styled after the world's three-plate pressure sequence: plate-w4-08-1/2/3 each need minMass 1.0 resting on them at once. With only two players, the solve is to park crate-w4-08-a on plate 1 and crate-w4-08-b on plate 2 (both carried the whole way from segment 2 for exactly this reason), freeing both players — one steps onto plate 3 to complete the AND (relay-w4-08-and, three inputs), which produces a momentary 'w4-08-gate-momentary'; relay-w4-08-hold (op delay, 2600ms) stretches that instant into a real window on 'w4-08-gate', consumed by door-w4-08-final, giving both players time to step off and cross together rather than needing a third body to hold the last plate forever. relic-w4-08 is picked up at spawn and carried the entire gauntlet for the haul objective, on top of the two crates — arriving with all three is the point. Four assist beams span every real fall gap, including one laid directly over the crumbly stretch for a player who'd rather skip its risk entirely; the crusher doorway and the plate sequence carry no beam, since neither is a fall hazard."
